      en: "Grand-Lahou Lagoon is a coastal lagoon in southeastern Côte d'Ivoire, near the town of Grand-Lahou. Part of the lagoon system along the Gulf of Guinea, it extends about 30 km and is separated from the Atlantic by a narrow sandbar. It is a vital ecosystem for waterbirds and fish. The water is brackish, with tidal influence. Local economy includes coconut and oil palm cultivation, and some tourism. The town of Grand-Lahou has about 15,000 inhabitants. The lagoon faces threats from pollution and overfishing.",
