      en: "Tiagba Lagoon is a small coastal lagoon in southeastern Côte d'Ivoire, near the village of Tiagba. Part of the Ébrié Lagoon system, it is about 10 km long, with mangroves and marshes. It is a crucial habitat for waterbirds and fisheries. The water is brackish. Surrounding villages rely on fishing and agriculture (coconuts, vegetables). The lagoon is relatively pristine but threatened by deforestation and erosion. It is a destination for ecotourism and birdwatching.",
